mation of plasma The process of Formation of cellular components of blood The destructive activity of red cells by the liver The reticulocytic destruction activity of red cells by spleen Is the formation of blood cellular components. All cellular blood components are derived from haematopoietic stem cells. Microcyte Acanthocyte Lacrimocytes Giant cell Burr cells Poikilocyte - A red blood cell of irregular shape. They have a segmented nucleus Their nucleus stains blue Their granules stain Blue Their cytoplasm contains pinkish granules Their granules overlap the nucleus Biconcave shape Very small nucleus Large amounts of hemoglobin Three layered cell membrane They have a life-span 3-4 months Which One of the following does NOT influence the specific gravity of blood CO2 Content Time of the day Blood Viscosity Total red cell count Colloidal plasma content The permeability of capillary wall is influenced by the following except one. pH Partial Pressure of Oxygen (PPO) Partial Pressure of Carbon dioxide (PPCO2) Hormones Size of red cells Hb F Hb C Hb S Hb E Both a and c 120 hours"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-94ffb351c2f9","stem":"4 weeks What is the importance of Vit. B12 in red blood cell formation? Removal of the nucleus For cell membrane formation For hemoglobin synthesis For Nucleic Acid synthesis For the red cell break down Hypochromic, Microcytic cells are? Large , normal red cell Large, less staining red cells Large , less staining Monocytes Small , normal Neutrophils Small cell with less hemoglobin PCV describes? The total red cell count in a volume of blood Relative mass of erythrocytes in a volume of blood Total blood cell in a blood volum