hich\\af42\\dbch\\af31505\\loch\\f42 regulation of cell differentiation"},{"label":"E","text":"\\par {\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\ltrpar \\rtlch\\fcs1 \\af42 \\ltrch\\fcs0 \\f42\\cf1 \\hich\\af42\\dbch\\af31505\\loch\\f42 c.\\tab}}\\pard \\ltrpar\\ql \\fi-360\\li720\\ri0\\nowidctlpar\\tx720\\wrapdefault{\\*\\pn \\pnlvlbody\\ilvl0\\ls42\\pnrnot0\\pnlcltr\\pnf42\\pnstart3\\pnindent360 {\\pntxta .}}"},{"label":"F","text":"\\faauto\\ls42\\rin0\\lin720\\itap0\\pararsid14355888 {\\rtlch\\fcs1 \\af42\\afs24 \\ltrch\\fcs0 \\f42\\fs24\\cf1\\insrsid10253861 \\hich\\af42\\dbch\\af31505\\loch\\f42 inhibition of viral differentiation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4b80aa2a13d3","stem":"Name=\"Project\"","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"HelpContextID=\"0\""},{"label":"B","text":"VersionCompatible32=\"393222000\""},{"label":"C","text":"CMG=\"FCFE1715EF15F315F315F315F3\""},{"label":"D","text":"DPB=\"F8FA13E414E414E4\""},{"label":"E","text":"GC=\"F4F61F1DE718E818E8E7\""}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","short_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ffe5656ea4fc","stem":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?>","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"<a:clrMap xmlns:a=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main\" bg1=\"lt1\" tx1=\"dk1\" bg2=\"lt2\" tx2=\"dk2\" accent1=\"accent1\" accent2=\"accent2\" accent3=\"accent3\" accent4=\"accent4\" accent5=\"accent5\" accent6=\"accent6\" hlink=\"hlink\" folHlink=\"folHlink\"/>"},{"label":"B","text":"\\Fë /*"},{"label":"C","text":"*€urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags"},{"label":"D","text":"€place"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d345471c620f51033193346114ce04085734c807"},{"id":"q-60ce3c0a4bef","stem":"Describe antigen processing and presentation of antigens from Epstein-Barr Virus (EBV) which has infected B cells. 4. You are sent a sample of human blood cells to analyze for MHC antigens. The genotype of the human donor is HLA-A 3+5+ and HLA-DR 1+2+. You remove the erythrocytes from the sample by Ficoll Hypaque density centrifugation and incubate aliquots of the cells with FITC-anti-DR1 or FITC anti-A5 and PE-anti-A3 or PE-anti-DR2. [FITC is a green fluorochrome and PE is a red fluorochrome.] After washing off unbound antibody, you analyze the surface MHC on your blood cells by flow cytometry. Complete flow cytometry plots for staining with a) FITC anti-DR1 and PE anti-A3, b) FITC anti-DR1 and PE anti-DR2, and c) FITC anti-A5 and PE anti-A3 by writing the names of the cells which will appear in each quadrant. Hint: Think about which cell types are in the blood and whether each cell type has Class I or Class II or both on its membrane. Cells positive for FITC fluorescence are in the top boxes, cells negative for FITC fluorescence in the bottom boxes. Cells positive for PE fluorescence are in the right-hand boxes, cells negative for PE fluorescence are in the left-hand boxes. 5. Influenza virus is an enveloped virus that infects primarily respiratory epithelial cells, but during the course of the infection respiratory tract DC also become infected and carry the virus to nearby lymphoid tissue, where they present it to lymphocytes. Describe how the virus would be processed and presented by these infected dendritic cells. To what cells would they present the antigens? What factors will influence how efficiently the antigens are presented? 6. In order to understand MH cells. The first is specific for peptide A presented on H-2k, and the second is specific for peptide B presented on H-2d. You then transfect cDNA for TCR from the cells of the first clone into cells from the second clone; the transfected T cells express both TCR molecules on each cell. Which of the following target cells would be killed by the transfected T cell clone and why? Target Cells Peptide","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["probable_document_or_multiple_questions","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["long_stem_manual_review","prior_structural_review_flag","probable_document_or_multiple_questions","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5d706e8c59a2","stem":". stem cells. 8. Which situation below describes an example of innate immunity?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"B","text":". antibody production by plasma cells."},{"label":"C","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"D","text":". antigen removal by cilia in the respiratory tract."},{"label":"E","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"F","text":". complement activation by antibody bound to the surface of a bacterium."}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e1b97170ec38","stem":". cytotoxic T cell binding and lysis of S. aureus. 25. Which of the following statements is FALSE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript"},{"label":"B","text":". An example of 0assive humoral immunity is treatment with horse anti-snace venin."},{"label":"C","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"D","text":". Antigen recognized by helper T cells must be associated with Class II MHC molecules on the surface of professional APC"},{"label":"E","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"F","text":". Each lymphocyte has many antigen binding receptnrs, each receptor capable of binding the sole antigen."}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicat