 of the following statements is FALSE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"B","text":". TCR is allelically excluded on individual T cells."},{"label":"C","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"D","text":". CD4 and CD8 co-receptors are also signal transducing molecules for T cell activation."},{"label":"E","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"F","text":". The arrangement of"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-79439860f54e","stem":"allogeneic kidney cells are CD8+ cytotoxic T cells. Problems 1. Like BCR, TCR have idiotypes. How could you prepare an anti-idiotype antibody to TCR that are specific for influenza virus hemagglutinin (HA), a protein on the envelope of influenza virus that binds RBC and causes them to agglutinate, restricted to HLA-B2.?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b3e98281a7c3","stem":". Peptides presented by Class I MHC must be 8-10 amino acids long. 24. 