,{"label":"D","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"E","text":". death of cells binding self antigen."},{"label":"F","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bfb1b1ac846e","stem":". requires the presence of RAG-1 and RAG-2. 9. Which of the following statements is TRUE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"B","text":". Isotypic exclusion on individual B cells pertains to expression of a single heavy chain isotype on each mature naive B cell."},{"label":"C","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"D","text":". Pre-B cells must receive a signal from specific antigen binding to pre-B receptor before they can proceed to the next stage in development."},{"label":"E","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"F","text":". Membrane"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d887792cc87d","stem":"immature B cells, mature B cells, neutrophils, macrophages? What would be the pattern of fluorescence you would see if you stained spleen cells with the same antibodies? Are the kinds of cells in each quadrant the same? HINT: consider all the kinds of leukocytes which are found in the spleen. How would this pattern change if you used mice lacking RAG-1 and RAG-2? 3. Make a line drawing of germline DNA and DNA from an early pro-B cell, a late pro-B cell, a large pre-B cell, and an immature B cell for both H","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c2bc5065ac67","stem":"quence must be H chain DNA in an immature B cell if ... A sequence must be germline L chain DNA if... A sequence must be L chain DNA in an early pro-B cell if ... A sequence must be L chain DNA in an late pro-B cell if ... A sequence must be L chain DNA in an immature B cell if ... Would the sequence be any different in a mature B cell? In a plasma cell secreting IgG1 in the lymph nodes? In a plasma cell secreting IgA2 in the MALT? 4. Starting with two cell lines from a mouse, one with cytotoxic activity and one with helper activity, how could you prepare and purify a rabbit anti-mouse CD4? 5. A transgenic mouse was constructed by inserting recombined H and L chain genes encoding an antibody to mouse H-Y antigen, which is expressed on the membrane of all cells of male but not female mice. Predict what B cell development will occur in male and in female transgenic mice. Describe or draw the flow cytometry data from spleen cells of male and of female mice stained with FITC-anti","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal"