-03d60bff89bc","stem":". contain infected T cells surrounded by macrophages. Problems 1. Leishmania major is a protozoan parasite that infects macrophages and monocytes, where it escapes destruction by lysosomal enzymes and escapes to replicate in vesicles. Different mouse strains respond differently to L. major infection: BALB/c mice produce primarily activated Th2 cells, while C57Bl/6 mice produce primarily activated Th1 cells. Which mouse strain would you expect to be more resistant to Leishmania infection, and why? What Leishmania-specific effector cells would be present in infected mice from each strain? 2. Design an experiment to prove that CTL are susceptible to perforin-mediated cytotoxicity HUMORAL IMMUNITY:- 1. T independent antigens do NOT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Psychiatry","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"B","text":". bind to BCR."},{"label":"C","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"D","text":". get presented on MHC Class II."},{"label":"E","text":"HYPERLINK \"javascript:;\""},{"label":"F","text":". have repeating epitopes."}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Psychiatry","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b429b52b603e","stem":". None of the above are true. 14. Which of the following is NOT a similarity between the cellular and humoral immune responses?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"HYPE