accent2=\"accent2\" accent3=\"accent3\" accent4=\"accent4\" accent5=\"accent5\" accent6=\"accent6\" hlink=\"hlink\" folHlink=\"folHlink\"/>"},{"label":"B","text":"*€urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags"},{"label":"C","text":"€place"},{"label":"D","text":"*€urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags"},{"label":"E","text":"€country-region"},{"label":"F","text":"a{D(Xq–öÿ"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d345471c620f51033193346114ce04085734c807"},{"id":"q-60f9a4c01e51","stem":"Define the following, -Hypnozoites, Gamete, Gametocyte, Gametogony, Erythrocytic Cycle, Chagas's Disease, 2. Contrast African Sleeping Sickness with Chagas' Disease. 3. Contrast the clinical picture for West African sleeping sickness to East African sleeping sickness. 4. Why is Trypanosoma lewisi not generally lethal to rats while Trypanosoma brucei is often lethal to cattle? 5. Contrast briefly the disease caused by Leishmania tropica with that cause by Leishmania donovani. 6. Contrast the type of reproduction utilized by members of the Phylum Apicomplexa with that utilized by the remaining parasitic protozoa. 7. What is the most primative morphological type of trypanosome; what is the most advanced? 8. Name the 4 species of Plasmodium to parasitize humans (list them in descending order according to numbers of humans infected; which species is most lethal; which species may remain with you for several years (more than 5). 9. How does Plasmodium and Toxoplasma evade the host's immune response? 10. List two reasons why Malaria is on the \"comeback\". 11. Describe briefly how the malaria life-cycle was identified, and what role each of the individuals below played in identifying the malaria life-cycle","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Louis Alphonse Laveran"},{"label":"B","text":"Patrick Manson"},{"label":"C","text":"Ronald Ross"},{"label":"D","text":"Amigo Bignami and Giovanni Grassi 12. 18. Draw a generalized Apicomplexa life-cycle. 13. . Why is both chloroquine and primaquin used in the treatment of malaria? 14. . Why is a serological test (such as ELISA) more necessary in the diagnosis of a Leishmania infection than a Trypanosome infection? 15. List 1 genus from each of the 3 phyla of parasitic protozoa that are considered to be commensials in the intestine. 16. List 2 protozoans that are commensials in human mouths. 17. Contrast the life-cycle of Sarcocystis to that of Plasmodium; what is the intermediate and definitive host for each? 18. How does Trypanosoma brucei gambiense trypomastigotes cause the characteristic symptoms of sleeping sickness? 19. What causes paroxyms in malaria patients? 20. Contrast the method by which malaria causes anemia to that of Trypanosoma brucei. 21. Contrast the method used by Trypanosoma cruzi to evade the immune response to that of Trypanosoma brucei. 22. List the four potential protozoans: a. _______________________________ b. _______________________________ c. _______________________________ d. _______________________________ 23. Chagas disease differs from African Sleeping Sickness in several clinically significant way. Describe 4 of these ways 24. Why is malaria often referred to as “black water fever”? What causes this condition? (Hint: what cells does malaria damage, and what is the secondary effects of that damage?) 25.Draw and label the monoxenous Apicomplexa life-cycle; making sure that you at least include the following terms: gametogony, macrogametocytes, merozoites, microgametocytes, oocysts, schizont, sporogony, sporozoites, trophozoites, and zygote 26. Describe in detail the physiological basis for the anemia and neurological symptoms associated with Trypanosoma brucei gambiense infections 27. Which four parasite forms are found in the life cycle of Trypanosoma brucei? 28.Name 4 differences between T. b. rhodesiense T. brucei gambiense and a)............................................................................................ b)............................................................................................... c)................................................................................................ d)................................................................................................... 29.In the life cycle of Plasmodium falciparum, the following stages are found in the liver cells: a)............................................................... b) .............................................................. c) .............................................................. And the following in the blood: a)............................................................... b) .............................................................. c) .............................................................. And the following in the Mosquito gut: a)............................................................... b) .............................................................. c) .............................................................. 30. a) In the life cycle of Trypanosoma brucei infective parasite forms injected into human body by tsetse are called ..................................... b) These transform into trypomastigotes with three forms c) Of these forms, which one causes infection in human host? .................................................. d) Multiplication parasite stages in the invertebrate host are(2)........................... e Infective parasite stage is ...................................................................... 31.What are the two trypanosome groups? (a)........................... (b) ....................... 32.Trypanasoma brucei rhodesiense is transimitted by ................................ while T. brucei gambiense is transimitted by ....................................... 33.Name three tsetse fly groups and associated diseases Group ........................... disease ................................... Group ........................... disease .................................. Group ...........................disease .................................. 34.Glossine (Tsetse) species are attracted to feeding on a host by the following a)......................................................... b) ........................................................ c) ....................................................... 35. control methods against tsetse flies include:- a).......................................................................... b)......................................................................... c)......................................................................... d) ....................................................................... e) ...................................................................... 36.Simple or complete metamorphosis is common with .................................. Trypanosomiasis vector. 37.Clinical features of American trypanosomiasis for acute phase are ......................................... and .................................................... 38. üñæÞñæÞæÞæÞñæÞæÞñæÞñæÞñæÐæÐæÞñæÐæÐæÞñæÞñæÞñæÐæÞæÐæÐæÞæÞñæÃæÞñæÞñæÃæÞñæÐæÐæÞñæ ÷ì÷ìÞìÞì÷ÖËÀ2À÷ÖËÀÖËÀ2ÀÖÀ2À2ÀÖ«§Ÿ«§›§«§«§“§“§‰§‚~ `„ˆðgd3/v öòöëòãÙöòÎòÄòÄòÎò1⁄4ò· ̄ò ̄ò¤TM‘†‚ °Ð/ °à=!° íuÕGtUäÂÿ /e \\ŠCÿ `„ ̃þo( `„ ̃þ‡h `„Lÿ‡h ^„Œ `„ ̃þ‡h"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displa