y his mom that he should not “leave the head” when removing a tick, and he is concerned about the outcome of this mistake. Please explain to your friend the following (20 total points)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Why is the term “head” not correct in this context? (3 points)"},{"label":"B","text":"On the back of this sheet, include a ventral perspective drawing of a female Ixodes tick, and label the following structures: hypostome, anus, spiracular plate, pedipalps, carapace (scutum), capitulum and walking legs. (10 points)"},{"label":"C","text":"Explain to your friend how to determine if this is a “Lyme Disease tick”. Include the appropriate structure(s) on your drawing. (3 points)"},{"label":"D","text":"Explain how your friend should have removed the tick. (4 points)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"99b4e090866f48c7e08b8a3b0a308973173c8a55"},{"id":"q-436d5c479fca","stem":"Cattle egrets which consume many insect pests from the backs of cattle are an example of which type of symbiosis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"mutualism"},{"label":"B","text":"commensalism"},{"label":"C","text":"phoresis"},{"label":"D","text":"parasitism"},{"label":"E","text":"predation"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitolo