 as crab lice due to the appearance of their middle and hind leg"},{"label":"E","text":"all of the statements are false"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bacdbfb80b2e","stem":"Identify the true statement.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the existence of \"life-cycles\" is not restricted to parasitic organisms"},{"label":"B","text":"both male and female mosquitoes take blood meals"},{"label":"C","text":"dog fleas cannot take blood meals from humans"},{"label":"D","text":"an organism cannot be both a vector for another parasite and a parasite itself"},{"label":"E","text":"the primary objective of most parasites is to kill their host 18 Which arthropod from the list below does not transmit any known disease."},{"label":"A","text":"Culex tarsalus"},{"label":"B","text":"Pediculus humanus humanus"},{"label":"C","text":"Phthirus pubis"},{"label":"D","text":"Glossina spp."},{"label":"E","text":"Dermacentor variabilis"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"09cf828910d08ea1da03e9c25d9a886b738795e9"},{"id":"q-ebdc00369790","stem":"Identify the false statement concerning Cimex spp.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cimex spp. is a blood sucker"},{"label":"B","text":"Most Cimex species are parasites of bats"},{"label":"C","text":"Cimex spp. have no wings"},{"label":"D","text":"Cimex spp. is a genus within the order Hemiptera"},{"label":"E","text":"Cimex spp. generally does not serve as a vector for any human diseases"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6d168a30df5e","stem":"Black flies or buffalo gnats .........","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"are of medical and/or economic importance because their larvae cause myiasis in humans and domestic animals"},{"label":"B","text":"are in the family Simuliidae"},{"label":"C","text":"are in the family Muscidae"},{"label":"D","text":"breed in temporary ponds"},{"label":"E","text":"are restricted to tropical areas of the world ORGANISM INTERMEDIATE HOST DEFINITIVE HOST MEANS OF INFECTION ENDEMIC COUNTRY (not USA) Ascaris lumbricoides Soil- Human Oncocerca volvulus Simulium damnosum Human dog encysted larvae in muscle Zaire V. Give two epidemiological factors associated with each of the following. (10 points)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d144fb0cd51db9169fa51685d113537208c7fead"},{"id":"q-a5fb219ea04a","stem":"Define the following and give example: (12marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Definitive host : The host in which the sexual reproduction of a parasite takes place - A host in which a parasite develops to an adult or sexually mature stage. Also called final host. E.g cat is the definitive host of T. gondii Example : the definitive hosts of T. gondii are cats"},{"label":"B","text":"Intermediate host The host ( animal or vector)occupied by juvenile stages of a parasite prior to the definitive host and in which asexual reproduction often occurs. -carry an infective stage Example: T.gondii intermediate hosts : sheep, goats, rodents, swine, cattle, chicken, and birds"},{"label":"C","text":"Reservoir host - An animal species which carries a pathogen without detriment to itself and serves as a source of infection. -an animal host that maintains a parasite life cycle in the wild, and functions as a source of the parasite for humans. -Refers to a host or carrier that harbors disease-causing organisms, without injury to itself and serves as a source from which other individuals can be infected. Example: Domestic Cats are the reservoir hosts of T.gondii"},{"label":"D","text":"Zoonosis: (2.5) - Zoonosis is any infectious disease that can be transmitted from animals, both wild and domestic, to humans. -Disease of animals that is transmissible to humans -An infection or infestation shared in nature by humans and other animals that are the normal or usual host; a disease of humans acquired from an animal source."},{"label":"E","text":"g Toxoplasmosis and Cryptosporidiosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Fecal oral route transmission Person-person transmission occurs by hand to mouth transfer of cysts from feces of an infected individual especially in institutions and daycare centres Examples"},{"label":"A","text":"Giardia lamblia"},{"label":"B","text":"Entamoeba histolytica"},{"label":"C","text":"Balantidium coli"},{"label":"D","text":"Cryptosporidium parvum"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","long_option_manual_review","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-109df1735a18","stem":"List species of protozoan parasites that you acquire by ingestion of undercooked meat. (1mark) Toxoplasma gondii","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8880f887c12f","stem":"Mention 4 mosquito control methods which involve the use of pesticides (4marks)","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","